description:
Design a frequency counter that measures the frequency of an input clock signal. The module increments a count on each rising edge of the clock input, then calculates the difference between successive counts to determine the frequency. Every time the count reaches 100 million, the current frequency value is outputted while resetting the counter for the next measurement cycle. The design effectively samples the frequency based on a predefined count threshold, yielding a frequency output in terms of clock cycles.
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  output reg [31:0] freq_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  output reg [31:0] freq_out
);reg [31:0] count = 0;
reg [31:0] prev_count = 0;
reg [31:0] diff = 0;
reg [31:0] freq = 0;

always @(posedge clk_in) begin
  count <= count + 1;
end

always @(posedge clk_in) begin
  if (count == 0) begin
    diff <= count - prev_count;
    prev_count <= count;
    freq <= diff;
  end
end

always @(posedge clk_in) begin
  if (count == 100000000) begin
    freq_out <= freq;
    freq <= 0;
    count <= 0;
  end
end

endmodule

