description:
Design a 4-bit linear feedback shift register (LFSR) counter that generates pseudo-random binary sequences. Upon receiving a clock signal, if enabled (ena), the circuit shifts the current state left and introduces feedback based on an XOR operation between the two most significant bits. The counter can be reset asynchronously to zero when the reset signal is low. The output reflects the current state of the register, allowing for the generation of a variable-length sequence of binary values based on the defined feedback configuration.
module top_module(
  input clk, reset, ena,
  output reg [SIZE-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk, reset, ena,
  output reg [SIZE-1:0] out
);parameter SIZE = 4;
  reg [SIZE-1:0] state;
  always @(posedge clk or negedge reset)
    begin
      if(!reset)
        state <= 0;
      else if(ena)
        state <= {state[SIZE-2:0], state[SIZE-1]^state[SIZE-2]};
    end
  assign out = state;
endmodule

