description:
Design a circuit that performs arithmetic shifting operations on a signed 32-bit input. The module takes a 7-bit instruction and a signed 32-bit operand as inputs. It extracts a 5-bit shift amount and a 2-bit shift type from the instruction. Depending on the shift type, the circuit can execute a logical left shift, a logical right shift, or an arithmetic right shift on the input operand, producing a 32-bit output reflecting the result of the selected shift operation.
