description:
Design a pipeline register with a configurable number of input and output signals, along with a specified depth. This module captures incoming data on each clock edge and shifts it through a series of flip-flops, effectively allowing for the storage and delayed output of signals. When provided with `n` input signals and `m` output signals, it leverages the `d` depth parameter to determine how many clock cycles the data will be delayed before being available at the output, thus facilitating data processing in a sequential manner commonly used in digital circuit design, particularly in synchronous systems.
module top_module(
  input clk,                 // added clock input
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output [m-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,                 // added clock input
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output [m-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of input signals
parameter m = 2; // number of output signals
parameter d = 4; // depth of pipeline register

reg [n-1:0] shift_reg [0:d-1]; // shift register implemented using flip-flops

integer i;

always @ (posedge clk) begin
  // shift input signals into shift register
  for (i = d-1; i > 0; i = i - 1) begin
    shift_reg[i] <= shift_reg[i-1];
  end
  shift_reg[0] <= in;
end

// output signals are the values stored in the flip-flops
assign out = shift_reg[d-1][m-1:0]; // ensure correct width for output

endmodule

