Design a circuit to compare the value of a 5-bit input, v1_reg_0, against a specific constant (which is interpreted as 9 in this case). The module utilizes two instances of a carry chain (CARRY4) to compute a sum based on the least and most significant bits. The output, comp1, indicates whether the input value is greater than or equal to 9, as it is set high when the resulting comparison sums to 1. The design effectively implements a binary comparator to evaluate the input against a predefined threshold.
module top_module(
    output reg comp1,
    input [4:0] v1_reg_0
);

